<!--
  navigate_igvc_autonav_humble.xml — IGVC AutoNav Challenge Behavior Tree

  Designed for ROS2 Humble + Navfn (GridBased) + MPPI (FollowPath) on the
  AndyMark Raptor tracked diff-drive chassis (0.7366 m gauge, 0.8 m radius).

  SYNTHESIS SOURCES:
    - TnTech IGVC 2026 (LCAS-Lab/TnTechIGVC2026 :: igvc_bt.xml) — base structure
    - Sooner Robotics 2024/2025 (SoonerRobotics/autonav_software_2024/2025) — orchestration pattern
    - Hosei orange_ros2 (KBKN-Autonomous-Robotics-Lab) — costmap-layer SetParameters
    - RoboJackets igvc-software — back_circle pattern (intentionally NOT adopted; MPPI PreferForwardCritic covers it)
    - IGVC 2026 Official Rules (igvc.org/2026rules.pdf, retrieved 2026-05-12)

  DESIGN PHILOSOPHY — "Dumb BT, smart orchestrator":
    - This BT executes ONE NavigateToPose at a time
    - A separate `mission_manager` Python node (to be implemented) owns:
        * waypoint cursor (lat/lon list, popped on 2.0 m proximity)
        * No-Man's-Land state machine (per-waypoint metadata tags)
        * GPS health watchdog (drop-to-dead-reckon at 2 s degraded, full
          forward-bias-only at 30 s lost)
        * SetParameters side-effects (toggle semantic_layer.lane_white,
          inflate goal_checker xy_tolerance, cap MPPI vx_max on ramp)
    - Orchestrator fires fresh NavigateToPose goals at 2 Hz with whatever
      goal is current; THIS BT is dumb — it just plans, follows, recovers.

  IGVC 2026 RULE-DRIVEN CONSTRAINTS encoded here:
    - 60 s Hold-up Traffic DQ                 -> outer Timeout msec=45000 (15 s margin)
    - 3-inch white-tape lane crossing penalty -> NO Spin (rectangular footprint sweeps
                                                  2.48 m diameter when off-center)
    - Remote control forbidden                -> NO AssistedTeleop
    - 1 mph minimum average over run          -> Wait capped at 2 s, recovery
                                                  budget 3 retries x 8 s = 24 s
    - Random obstacles every run              -> ComputePathToPose (not ComputeRoute);
                                                  campus GeoJSON graph reserved for testing
    - Mandatory payload, e-stop, safety light -> handled at orchestrator level,
                                                  not in this BT

  RECOVERY ORDER (per design-agent analysis):
    1+2. ClearLocal + ClearGlobal     (zero-motion, free, no DQ risk)
    3.   Wait wait_duration=2          (exploits kiwicampus semantic_layer
                                        tile_map_decay_time=1.5 + Velodyne
                                        raytrace at 10 Hz to clear stale cells)
    4.   BackUp 0.3 m @ 0.08 m/s       (3.75 s; retraces known-clear arc;
                                        half of TnTech's 0.5 m to keep robot
                                        inside planning window)
    5.   DriveOnHeading 0.15 m @ 0.10  (1.5 s; nudges through borderline
                                        passages that MPPI rejected)

  REQUIRES (Phase 5 validation will enforce):
    - bt_navigator.plugin_lib_names MUST include:
        nav2_back_up_action_bt_node
        nav2_drive_on_heading_bt_node
      (everything else is already present in nav2_params_humble.yaml)
    - behavior_server.behavior_plugins MUST include backup, drive_on_heading,
      wait (already present per nav2_params_humble.yaml).
    - Timeout, Sequence, ReactiveFallback, RoundRobin are BT.CPP v3 builtins
      and need no plugin registration.

  HOW TO USE:
    ros2 launch avros_bringup navigation.launch.py \
      bt_xml:=navigate_igvc_autonav_humble.xml
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">

    <!-- OUTER WATCHDOG: hard-abort the whole navigation action after 45 s.
         IGVC Hold-up Traffic rule fires at 60 s — 15 s margin lets the
         action FAILURE bubble up to the mission_manager, which can either
         skip the current waypoint or signal the operator-held wireless
         e-stop. Without this, a wedged MPPI could burn the full 60 s and
         disqualify the run on a single stuck waypoint. -->
    <Timeout msec="45000">

      <!-- OUTER RECOVERY: 3 retries. Each retry runs the recovery sub-tree
           (~8 s) then re-enters the plan-follow pipeline. 3 x 8 s = 24 s
           well under the 45 s Timeout. After 3 failures the Timeout will
           catch us via the FAILURE return. -->
      <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="3" name="NavigateRecovery">

        <!-- MAIN PIPELINE: replan + follow, with per-step recovery.
             No RateController — orchestrator fires fresh goals at 2 Hz
             (TnTech pattern); replan only on planner failure, not on a
             timer, to avoid stale path while a fresh one is computed. -->
        <PipelineSequence name="NavigateWithReplanning">

          <!-- PLAN step. 2026-05-12: wrapped in RateController hz=1.0 per
               canonical Humble pattern in navigate_to_pose_w_replanning_and_recovery.xml.
               Without the rate gate, PipelineSequence re-ticks the planner at the
               full BT rate (~10 Hz), causing path thrashing and wasted CPU.
               Inner RecoveryNode(retries=1) clears the GLOBAL costmap if Navfn
               fails — stale semantic_layer marks from old camera frames are the
               most common failure mode on this stack (kiwicampus tile_map_decay_time=1.5
               + raytrace patch usually resolves them, but a forced clear unblocks
               the planner immediately). -->
          <RateController hz="1.0">
            <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="ComputePathToPose">
              <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}"
                                 path="{path}"
                                 planner_id="GridBased"/>
              <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Context"
                service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
            </RecoveryNode>
          </RateController>

          <!-- FOLLOW step. 2026-05-12: inner ClearLocal removed — when MPPI
               correctly refused to cross a lane, the clear wiped the lane
               from the costmap and MPPI then drove through the now-empty
               area before perception could re-mark it. FollowPath failures
               now bubble straight to the outer recovery sub-tree, which
               has a 2s Wait before retrying (lets perception re-fill). -->
          <FollowPath path="{path}"
                      controller_id="FollowPath"
                      goal_checker_id="general_goal_checker"/>

        </PipelineSequence>

        <!-- RECOVERY SUB-TREE: runs ONLY if PipelineSequence returns FAILURE
             after its own inner retries are exhausted (i.e. ClearGlobal +
             replan didn't fix it AND ClearLocal + re-follow didn't fix it).

             ReactiveFallback aborts the recovery the moment the goal
             changes — GoalUpdated returns SUCCESS as soon as the
             orchestrator publishes a new carrot, so an in-flight BackUp
             stops and the next plan-follow cycle starts fresh. -->
        <ReactiveFallback name="RecoveryFallback">
          <GoalUpdated/>

          <!-- 2026-05-12: Sequence → RoundRobin per canonical Humble pattern
               in navigate_to_pose_w_replanning_and_recovery.xml. RoundRobin
               cycles through children on successive recovery invocations
               (1st = ClearAroundRobot, 2nd = Wait, 3rd = BackUp, 4th = CrawlForward,
               then wraps). With outer RecoveryNode number_of_retries=3 we get
               three escalating attempts before failing the goal. The previous
               Sequence ran ALL steps every invocation (re-clearing every time
               and aborting mid-way if any step FAILED — DriveOnHeading
               sometimes never ran).

               2026-05-12: also dropped the unconditional ClearEntireCostmap
               on the global costmap — same lane-wipe race we just fixed at
               the inner FollowPath level. The painted lane is persistent,
               so wiping the global costmap forces the next planner tick to
               route THROUGH where the lane was until perception re-marks it.
               Replaced with ClearCostmapAroundRobot (resets only the cells
               near the robot — preserves distant lane markings).

               Spin still deliberately omitted: rectangular footprint
               (1.0 x 0.74 m) sweeps a 2.48 m diameter circle when off-center,
               exceeding the half-lane width (~1.5 m) and risking IGVC DQ. -->
          <RoundRobin name="LaneAwareRecoveryActions">

            <ClearCostmapAroundRobot name="ClearAroundRobot-Recovery"
              service_name="local_costmap/clear_around_local_costmap"
              reset_distance="3.0"
              server_timeout="5000"/>

            <Wait wait_duration="2" name="WaitForSemanticDecay"/>

            <!-- 2026-05-29 (Phase 0): backup_dist 1.5->0.3, backup_speed 0.08->0.10.
                 The 1.5 m was a latent bug: it contradicted this BT's own header
                 comment ("BackUp 0.3 m"), took 18.75 s @ 0.08 m/s (over the 24 s
                 recovery budget), and — with NO rear sensor — drove blind past the
                 rear lane boundary (no costmap cells behind base_link to stop it).
                 0.3 m stays inside the robot's own footprint-clear zone that MPPI
                 already verified. Structural fix (back_circle rear-exclusion layer)
                 is Phase 4 of nav2_cohort_strategy.md. -->
            <BackUp backup_dist="0.3"
                    backup_speed="0.10"
                    time_allowance="25"
                    name="ShortBackup"/>

            <DriveOnHeading dist_to_travel="0.15"
                            speed="0.10"
                            time_allowance="10"
                            name="CrawlForward"/>

          </RoundRobin>
        </ReactiveFallback>

      </RecoveryNode>
    </Timeout>

  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
